Paper Rock Scissors

A simple Python command-line game where the player competes against the computer in Rock, Paper, Scissors.

Features

- Player can choose Rock, Paper, or Scissors.
- The computer randomly selects one of the three choices.
- The program determines the winner based on the game rules.
- Handles invalid player inputs.
- Supports exiting the game by entering "EXIT".
- Detects draws when both the player and computer choose the same option.

Game Rules

- Rock beats Scissors
- Scissors beats Paper
- Paper beats Rock
- Same choices result in No Winners

How to Run

Make sure Python is installed on your computer.

Run the following command:

python Paper_Rock_Scissors.py

Then enter your choice when prompted.

Valid Choices

Rock
Paper
Scissors
EXIT

The program is not case-sensitive, so inputs such as "rock", "ROCK", and "Rock" are accepted.

Technologies Used

- Python
- "random" module
- "while" loop
- "if / elif / else" statements
- User input
- String methods

